<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="S4.T4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">An empirical time analysis comparing the AVB method and our proposed IVRS on the MNIST dataset. GPU-accelerated parallelization is able to reduce the impact of additional computation required by our method.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To evaluate the efficiency of our model, we conducted an empirical time analysis comparing IVRS to the baseline AVB on MNIST. The results are shown in Table <a href="#S4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 4.4 Variational Autoencoder Task on MNIST ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Implicit Variational Rejection Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. Using a batch size of 64 during training, we observed that our model incurs only a slight increase in computational cost, showing the advantage of our GPU-accelerated parallel sampling implementation.</p>
</div>
