</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We have introduced Implicit Variational Rejection Sampling, a novel posterior approximation method that enhances variational inference by integrating the flexibility of implicit distributions with the precision of rejection sampling. By optimizing the derived Implicit Resampled Evidence Lower Bound (IR-ELBO), IVRS provides a mechanism for enhancing posterior approximation over traditional VI methods. Our experimental results demonstrate the effectiveness of IVRS across various tasks, including regression problems and VAE-based image modeling, achieving superior quantitative performance over related inference approaches. The supplement below contains more practical details about implementation and limitations, along with an in depth description of related work and ablation study.</p>
</div>
